How many comparisons does binary search make to find 23? (The program prints the count.)

int[] a = {2, 5, 8, 12, 16, 23, 38, 56, 72, 91};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, c = 0;
while (lo <= hi) {
    int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
    c++;
    if (a[mid] == 23) break;
    else if (a[mid] < 23) lo = mid + 1;
    else hi = mid - 1;
}
System.out.println(c);

